{
    "architecture": "x86_64",
    "context": "Native musl ELF64 root/UID1000: 430 range/length/error/count checks across regular files, pipes, UNIX stream/datagram sockets and 2/8/9/513/1024-entry imports. Fixed mmap probes measure the active address limit (47-bit ARM, 56-bit x86 QEMU), map its last page and refuse the next. Unchanged kernels fail 121 cases per credential cohort and consume/mutate original resources; fixed kernels preserve offsets, bytes and queues. EOF boundary tests verify one-segment page-size MAX_RW_COUNT truncation before range checks; multi-segment original ranges and zero tails are checked before I/O. Two 200-cycle error/count cohorts retain flat slab classes/big pages; header/descriptor race cases remain passing. Eleven cases pass; x86 uses seven completed cases plus four resumed cases against the identical frozen kernel, preserving its original failed sharedmem staging row. Host/geometry checks pass; existing allocation allowances still fail identically. No 2 GiB payload transfer, positioned vectors, tagged ARM addresses, four-level x86 run, shared-offset atomicity, stream message conformance, exhaustion or foreign ABI qualification",
